-- title:
--   Germs at a supersingular crossing are node-integral
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$ and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of properness, flatness, integrality and normality data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\mathbb Z$ with Igusa coordinate `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, together with its rational and geometric curve models, their Galois compatibilities, the two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ and a smooth locus. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, $K$ its fraction field, and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring homomorphism; write $\mathfrak X_O$ for the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, assumed integral, and let $x$ be a point of $\mathfrak X_O$. Let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field `modularFunctionFieldBar` applied to $1 * p$ (the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficient-embedded full modular function field of level $p$), subject to two normalisations: on constants, $\varphi$ sends the germ at $x$ of the global section attached to $a \in O$ to the image of $\iota_K(a)$; and on the finite chart, whose preimage under the first projection is assumed nonempty, $\varphi$ sends the germ of the section attached to $a$ in `chartAlgFin ℤ` (the elements of the level-$p$ modular function field integral over $\mathbb Z[j]$) to the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of $a$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a perfect algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, $red : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism, `data` a `ModularPolynomialData p` satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, and $h_\alpha, h_\beta$ the integrality of the two level-raising maps from level $1$ to level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization A p 1 data hKr k red hα hβ` and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple P`, with its two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`. Assume $\iota_K(O) \subseteq A$ and that $to\kappa : O \to k$ is the induced reduction, $to\kappa(a) = red(\iota_K(a))$. Assume both branch generic points specialise to $x$: the images under `𝔛.compInf k` followed by base change along $to\kappa$, and under `𝔛.compZero k` followed by the same base change, of the generic point of the curve $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ both specialise to $x$. Let $w$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` over $k$ lying in `ssPlaces p 1 k`, and assume the $j$-value pin: there is $\hat\jmath \in O$ with $red(\iota_K(\hat\jmath))$ equal to the evaluation at $w$ of the level-one generator `jGeomGen k 1`, and an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at $x$ with $\varphi(t) = \mathrm{jFun}\,1\,p - \iota_K(\hat\jmath)$. Then for every $s$ in that stalk, $\varphi(s)$ lies in the subring `R.nodeIntegers w`, that is, $\varphi(s)$ belongs to the integers of $R_1$, to the integers of $R_2$, and to the valuation subring of every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `P.reduceFst V = w`.
--
--   This is one half of the dictionary between regularity on the Deligne–Rapoport model at a supersingular crossing of its characteristic-$p$ fibre and node-integrality on the level-$p$ modular function field: germs at the crossing read, through $\varphi$, into the node ring attached to the supersingular place $w$. It feeds the construction of node coordinates at such a crossing and the computation of the crossing width in terms of the $j$-invariant.
